      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It was shown that during 24 h following whole-body exposure of male rats to gamma-quanta (150 Gy) the latent period of their response to the thermal effect increased a \"tail-flick\" test) and the threshold of the nociceptive response to an electric stimulus (the vocalization threshold) decreased. A correlation was found between the initial response to the nociceptive effects and variation of these values in irradiated animals."},
